#: ../../.opencode/skills/debugging-investigation/SKILL.md:10
msgid "Core approach"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/debugging-investigation/SKILL.md:12
msgid "Reproduce the problem if feasible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/debugging-investigation/SKILL.md:13
msgid "Gather evidence before drawing conclusions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/debugging-investigation/SKILL.md:14
msgid "Separate observations, hypotheses, and confirmed root causes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/debugging-investigation/SKILL.md:15
msgid "Narrow the failure surface methodically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/debugging-investigation/SKILL.md:16
msgid "Prefer the smallest fix that addresses the actual cause."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/debugging-investigation/SKILL.md:18
msgid "Practical guidance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/debugging-investigation/SKILL.md:20
msgid ""
"**Ground before you guess.** Before proposing a diagnosis, fix, or "
"design, enumerate the load-bearing claims it depends on (what specific "
"code does, what payloads contain, where errors originate, how working "
"siblings of the same shape behave). Mark each `read` (you've inspected "
"the actual source in this session) or `assumed`. Read the assumed ones — "
"or downgrade the proposal to \"still investigating\" — before writing it "
"down. Output the claim list visibly in your summary. A proposal that "
"departs structurally from working in-tree siblings of the same shape "
"(plugin, provider, integration, form, migration, adapter, command) treats"
" the deviation as the first hypothesis to disprove, not a feature."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/debugging-investigation/SKILL.md:21
msgid ""
"Look at logs, tests, stack traces, configuration, recent changes, and "
"runtime assumptions together."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/debugging-investigation/SKILL.md:22
msgid ""
"Pay attention to environment differences, race conditions, stale state, "
"and boundary failures."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/debugging-investigation/SKILL.md:23
msgid "When reproduction is incomplete, be explicit about what is inferred."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/debugging-investigation/SKILL.md:24
msgid ""
"Trace the complete end-to-end code flow — from user interaction or "
"trigger through every layer to where the bug manifests. Do not stop at "
"the immediate method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/debugging-investigation/SKILL.md:25
msgid "Read every file in the flow. Do not skim or assume."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/debugging-investigation/SKILL.md:26
msgid ""
"Look for secondary defects in the same flow — other bugs that aren't the "
"reported issue but would cause problems."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/debugging-investigation/SKILL.md:27
msgid ""
"Check all code paths that could trigger the issue (different input "
"formats, config modes, error handling branches)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/debugging-investigation/SKILL.md:29
msgid "Investigation report template"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/debugging-investigation/SKILL.md:31
msgid ""
"Use this template when documenting investigation findings. All sections "
"are required unless explicitly not applicable. Add additional sections "
"for information that doesn't fit the template."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/debugging-investigation/SKILL.md:33
msgid ""
"## Summary\n"
"\n"
"### Categorization\n"
"| Attribute | Assessment |\n"
"|-----------|------------|\n"
"| **Criticality** | [critical/high/medium/low] — [short explanation] |\n"
"| **Ease of Fix** | [easy/moderate/hard] — [short explanation] |\n"
"| **Caused by our codebase?** | [Yes/No] — [short explanation] |\n"
"| **Needs more research?** | [Yes/No] — [short explanation] |\n"
"\n"
"### Background\n"
"[Simple text description of what this bug is, its complexity, "
"criticality, and estimated fix effort]\n"
"\n"
"### Analysis\n"
"[Simple description of why it is occurring]\n"
"\n"
"### Root Cause\n"
"[Simple description of the root cause]\n"
"\n"
"### Source\n"
"[Simple description of what code is involved]\n"
"\n"
"### Fix Direction\n"
"[Simple description of what is needed to fix the issue — high level only,"
" no implementation details]\n"
"\n"
"---\n"
"\n"
"## Problem Statement\n"
"[Full research details on the issue and cause. Include reproduction steps"
" if available. Reference specific error messages, logs, stack traces.]\n"
"\n"
"## Environment Details\n"
"[List any relevant setup, config, or environmental details or factors. If"
" not applicable, say so.]\n"
"\n"
"---\n"
"\n"
"## Root Cause Analysis\n"
"[Full root cause analysis with evidence. Cite specific code, conditions, "
"and data that prove the root cause. Separate confirmed findings from "
"hypotheses.]\n"
"\n"
"---\n"
"\n"
"## Code Flow (End to End)\n"
"[Numbered list of the complete code flow from the entry point (user "
"interaction, API call, job trigger) through every layer to where the bug "
"manifests. Include file paths and line numbers at each step.]\n"
"\n"
"1. `path/to/file.ext:NN` — [what happens at this step]\n"
"2. `path/to/file.ext:NN` — [next step in the flow]\n"
"3. ...\n"
"\n"
"---\n"
"\n"
"## Key Files\n"
"\n"
"[Group by logical area. Each area gets a table.]\n"
"\n"
"### [Area name, e.g., \"API Layer\" or \"Storage Service\"]\n"
"| File | Lines | Relevance |\n"
"|------|-------|-----------|\n"
"| `path/to/file.ext` | NN–MM | [description of relevance] |\n"
"\n"
"### [Next area]\n"
"| File | Lines | Relevance |\n"
"|------|-------|-----------|\n"
"| `path/to/file.ext` | NN–MM | [description of relevance] |\n"
"\n"
"---\n"
"\n"
"## Secondary Defects\n"
"[Other bugs or concerns discovered during investigation that aren't the "
"reported issue but exist in the same code flow. If none found, state "
"\"None identified.\"]\n"
"\n"
"---\n"
"\n"
"## Notes\n"
"[Any additional observations, context, or concerns not covered above]\n"
"\n"
"---\n"
"\n"
"## Recap\n"
"[2-3 sentence recap of the investigation: what the bug is, what causes "
"it, and how severe it is]\n"
msgstr ""

